<h1>Archie/Namagati/Odivair</h1>
<h6>©Gordon Bok</h6>

<p>        <i>Three stray tunes of mine. The first
was written thinking about Archie Fisher,
and how he was always flaming around
whenever I saw him. It's properly
called "Archie, Take Your Boots Off and
Stop Chasing Yourself Around." "Namagati" (a direction of wind) is a dance
from "Song for Vela" which appeared as
a guitar duet with John Pearse on Another
Land Made of Water (Folk-Legacy FSI-72).
"Odivair is a Lonely Man" is one of
the many tunes I put to the old Shetlandish saga : The Play of the Lady
Odivere . (GB)  </i>

</p>

